    {
      "id": "1jg5qx9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Characteristics of Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plants are multicellular, eukaryotic autotrophs with cellulose-based cell walls.",
        "Plant tissues are divided into Meristematic (actively dividing) and Permanent tissues (Xylem and Phloem).",
        "Photosynthesis synthesizes glucose and oxygen using light, carbon dioxide, and water inside chloroplasts.",
        "Plant reproduction occurs through sexual mechanisms in flowers and asexual mechanisms via vegetative propagation.",
        "Phytohormones including Auxins, Gibberellins, Cytokinins, Abscisic Acid, and Ethylene regulate plant growth and development."
      ],
      "id": "ygroudh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mmpvzu3",
      "content": "• Plants are multicellular eukaryotic organisms."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2mfnkyu",
      "content": "• They contain chlorophyll and perform photosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r3l4bz0",
      "content": "• Cell walls are made of cellulose."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tkq7xz9",
      "content": "• They are generally non‑motile."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jfpipc1",
      "content": "• They store food mainly in the form of starch."
    },
