    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Xylem transports water unidirectionally, whereas Phloem transports food bidirectionally.",
        "Ethylene is the only natural plant hormone that exists in a gaseous state and regulates fruit ripening.",
        "Bryophytes are commonly referred to as the 'amphibians of the plant kingdom' as they require water for reproduction.",
        "The Light Reaction of photosynthesis occurs in the Grana, while the Dark Reaction takes place in the Stroma."
      ],
      "id": "b2vh863"
